From 7fde3cd2220d944e875d4e64edb9e81b6277111a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Steele <jonathan@renew-it.us>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:54:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] SD Erlang s_groups: build s_group with the kernel
 (Makefile MODULES)

The kernel Makefile compiles only the modules it lists; s_group was in
kernel.app.src but not in MODULES, so a source build (./configure && make)
installed a kernel whose supervisor could not start s_group (undef). The
container images compiled the changed modules separately and missed it;
found by bin/sd-host-build.
---
 lib/kernel/src/Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/lib/kernel/src/Makefile b/lib/kernel/src/Makefile
index bc94e3d..a4d6e17 100644
--- a/lib/kernel/src/Makefile
+++ b/lib/kernel/src/Makefile
@@ -143,6 +143,7 @@ MODULES = \
 	pg2 \
 	ram_file \
 	rpc \
+	s_group \
 	seq_trace \
 	socket \
 	standard_error \
-- 
